# Narset's Reversal returns the spell to its owner's hand; that is not countering it (CR 701.6), so Bot2's Abrupt Decay,
# which can't be countered, goes too. Bot2 aims the Decay at Bot1's Mox Sapphire; Bot1 copies it at Bot2's Mox Jet. The
# copy destroys the Jet, and the original is in Bot2's hand, so the Sapphire stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Island
Narset's Reversal
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Forest
Abrupt Decay
Forest x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Abrupt Decay.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Narset's Reversal.Cast(Stack.Abrupt Decay)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet)
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Types = Artifact
Bot2.Graveyard = Mox Jet
Bot2.Hand.Abrupt Decay.Colors = Black; Green
Stack.Count = 0
